WEBVTT

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:03.480
Daiki.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.810
Daiki, wake up. Come on.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.340
I've got your favorite chocolate.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.240
I'll eat it all if you don't wake up.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.480
Wake up.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.420
Wake up, Daiki.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.680
I'll give you my half, too, so wake up.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.020
Wake up.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:27.160
A dream?

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.260
Oh, shoot!

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.420
I'm leaving now!

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.960
And you're up!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.480
Our campaign for the main election starts today.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.230
We don't have a second to waste on sleep.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.020
Come on, hurry up.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.580
Do I need to help you change,

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.590
Daiki?

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:00.990
What's wrong, Yuuki?

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.800
What are you staring at?

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.460
Huh? Oh, nothing.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.220
Get up already, Yuuki.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.350
Accident!<b>
We, the Public Safety Commission,</b>

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.240
We, the Public Safety Commission,

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.890
have been the ruling party for many years now.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:52.080
However, we've unfortunately been forced to withdraw from the election this year

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.200
as a result of the incident involving Commissioner Oosawa.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.260
As maintaining our rule is no longer an option,

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.060
we must begin planning for next year's election immediately.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.660
There are three candidates this year.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.820
From the Finance Commission, we have Shinonome Satsuki,

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.920
and from the General Affairs Commission, we have Tatsumi Moheiji.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.700
As we know from our experience, the ruling party has the advantage in an election.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:21.060
If we allow any other commission to ascend,

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.510
our prospects for next year's election will be dim.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.020
However,

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:32.260
if the independent candidate Oojima Yuuki, who has no supporting party, is elected President...

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.540
The Public Safety Commission will support Oojima Yuuki.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.300
One of our officers, an intelligence operative, is already on detail.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:44.320
Take care not to let anyone learn of this.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.030
Especially not...

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:48.700
the Katahira faction.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.820
You should've printed the flyers <i>before</i> we had to leave!

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.940
That's not the candidate's job!

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.720
We're understaffed!

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.180
You could've just had Yume do this—

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.580
I'm sorry! I didn't see you!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.810
Are you okay?

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.310
I'm completely fine.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.880
Are you sure?

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:18.180
Oh, are you a candidate?

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.620
Oh, yeah, I am.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.000
Maybe you've heard of me.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.740
I'm the first candidate not from any of the three commissions to pass the primaries in seven years.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.240
Nope.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.680
No one knows about you because you're not working hard enough.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.750
I'm sorry. I haven't been to school in a while, so I don't know much about the election.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.680
Oh, that explains it.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.170
My name's Oojima. Oojima Yuuki!

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:45.680
Oojima Yuuki-san? You have a very nice name.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.380
Thank you very much!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.720
I'm running for <i>true</i> reform!

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.180
I hope you'll lend me your support!

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.440
Yes, of course.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.740
You were laying the nice guy act on pretty thick back there.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:01.480
I have to get along with the voters.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.200
So it's not because she's a girl?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.360
What are you—

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.320
Isn't that...

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.370
That was a dirty trick!

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.720
Don't blame me because you didn't notice sooner.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.370
You always do things like this!

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:18.040
You should analyze your opponent better next time.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:22.590
Keep getting distracted that easily, and someone
might pull the rug out from under your feet.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.800
Nee-san!

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.320
Good morning, Sneakyjima-kun.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.810
Where did that name come from?!

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:35.240
Because you were eavesdropping on our conversation like a sneak.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:35.940
You don't like it?

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.190
Of course not!

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:43.500
So what's the matter this time?
I thought you made up with Sensei.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.960
She tricked me.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:45.530
Huh?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.700
That match was mine!

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.300
Match? Do you mean the shogi game from yesterday?

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.240
Yeah.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.020
When I played out the game again at home,

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.580
I realized that I had mate in just a few moves!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.560
I see...

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.720
I was so wrapped up in her story.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:06.880
She must've started talking about the past to distract me!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.400
You <i>wanted</i> to find out about her past,

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.970
so does it really matter who won?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.340
That's not the issue here!

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.180
You were the prize for that match...

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.660
No, never mind.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.110
Never mind what?

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.000
What are you guys talking about?

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.730
Well, nothing much.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:27.220
Is she on your campaign staff?

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.070
Yes, my campaign manager.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:34.740
We're not making secret agreements or doing anything in regards to the election, so don't worry.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.000
Yup, it's just as she says.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.880
We were having a conversation concerning private matters.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.250
Yup, it's just as— Huh?!

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.800
D-Don't call it "private"!

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.560
What's wrong, Chisato?

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.300
Nothing.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.700
Why are you so angry?

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.920
I'm not angry!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.240
Yes, you are.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.260
I just said that I'm not!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.480
I <i>told</i> you,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.270
I wasn't discussing anything election-related with Shinonome-san!

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.020
That's why I'm angry!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.520
See? You're angry.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.420
Oh, you!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.040
You're late!

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.800
Why did it take you forever to bring those flyers?!

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.540
Hurry up before the other students start showing up!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.380
Sorry. Something came up on the way over.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.800
Yuu-kun, thanks for yesterday.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:22.330
Huh?

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.360
Satsuki and I managed to resolve the bad blood between us.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.260
Thank you.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.720
Oh, I didn't do anything.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.340
Oh, no. It wouldn't have happened without you.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:34.700
I'm grateful.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:36.420
You're too kind.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:38.470
Attention, everyone!

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.480
The main attraction of the day...

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:41.940
Switch on!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.860
Go... Change!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.580
Shoot!

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:08.420
This is Non-chan's invention, Stage Champion!

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.430
But it really is just as President Mouri told us.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:16.980
Most of the students will see us as they're coming to school.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.680
Waking up early was worth it!

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.080
You claimed this spot for us, Mii-chan?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.820
I did. I can't do much manual labor, so this is one of the few things I can help with.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.190
Mii-chan!

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.190
Catch me!

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.650
Wait!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.530
Got you!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.820
No fair, Onee-chan!

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.030
Is too!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.000
Mii-chan, I love you!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.400
Will you go out with me?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.840
Yuu-kun, I'm flattered,

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:53.700
but I'm in love with someone else.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:56.800
Huh?

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.600
Chisato?

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:03.520
Y-Yeah! Let's hand out these flyers, guys!

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:08.020
Are you giving a street speech here today?

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.580
Shiohama-san!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:14.960
The ASP assigned me to report on you throughout the election!

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.110
I look forward to working with you.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:20.460
Same here. Let's do our best!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.330
Th-Thanks.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:25.620
Flyer team, are we all set?

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.250
I'm ready any time!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:28.130
Normal.

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:30.760
What should we be doing?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.760
I have a very special job, just for you two!

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.540
If you put it that way...

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.340
...there's no way we can refuse!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.180
So what do you want us to do?!

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.060
I want you to power the equipment!

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:45.770
Power it?

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:47.520
All right, guys.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.480
Let's get started!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.900
Yeah!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:50.980
Yeah.

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:19.760
Gentlemen!

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:25.140
Public Safety's fall from power this year is our opportunity to rise!

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:27.380
We must not let it go to waste!

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:29.500
Make every second count!

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.270
Yes, sir!

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:33.880
We have a very influential ally this year.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.960
There's nothing for us to fear.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.130
I'll stop the club reforms!

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:51.610
I need your support!

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.920
Please support Oojima Yuuki!
I need your support!

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:53.960
I need your support!

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.300
Please vote for Oojima Yuuki!

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:01.010
Oojima Yuuki, the true independent candidate, is here to revolutionize the school!

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:02.740
Oojima...

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.150
Yuuki...

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:05.010
wants your vote.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.900
Please vote for Oojima Yuuki!

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.520
What's this?

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.770
Financial aid students work in election campaigns, too?

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.400
No way! Students on aid have the right to vote?

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.400
Please give those back!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.580
That would be a problem, wouldn't it?

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:20.650
Please, give them back!

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:21.210
I will...

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.120
Please!
I will...

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:22.660
Please!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.660
I need that!

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.920
<i>Aomi-san!</i>

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:29.750
Yuuki?

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.220
Stop it! Please!

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:35.340
What the hell? This guy wants better treatment for people on financial aid?

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.160
I hope that doesn't mean using <i>our</i> money.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:39.260
Hey!

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.240
Oojima-senpai...

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:42.760
What are you doing to her?

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.360
What's the big deal? She's on financial aid.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.660
You're siding with students on financial aid?

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.520
You got a problem with us?

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:50.920
You guys...

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.560
Stop it, Yuuki! You're campaigning!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.860
Don't do anything violent!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:55.820
But...

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.070
Hold it in for now. I'm begging you.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.100
That's enough.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.220
We're with the Public Safety Commission.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:07.800
Show us see your student IDs, please.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.450
We haven't done anything wrong!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.620
Your student IDs, <i>please</i>.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.860
W-We haven't done anything wrong!

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.880
We saw everything.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.250
Your student IDs, please.

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.260
They match their owners.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:29.420
Student code section seven, relationships with other students, item two:

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:33.620
Respect other people, regardless of their age, gender, or status.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:35.900
And item three: Violence will not be tolerated.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:40.780
We suspect that you are in violation of the aforementioned items.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.440
We haven't done anything violent!

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:47.320
Verbal abuse, which can affect others psychologically, is equivalent to violence.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:48.940
We will follow up on this later.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:50.700
Report to the Public Safety Commission when summoned.

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.220
What's the matter?

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:03.220
It's all right. It's over now.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.970
Are you okay, Aomi-san?

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.300
Yes, thank you.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.180
I can handle this much.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.220
I'm used to it.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:15.200
I was actually more frightened by the Public Safety Commission.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:15.980
The Public Safety Commission?

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:20.180
One time, a financial aid student in my class was taken away by the Public Safety Commission,

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.700
and they left her traumatized.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:27.490
It was so bad that she stopped coming to school.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:31.240
Is that the girl involved in the Oosawa Incident?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:40.980
An anonymous source tipped off the Public Safety Commission that a financial aid student

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:42.760
had shoplifted from the school store.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:47.300
Public Safety Commissioner Oosawa overstepped her bounds during the investigation

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:51.260
and even disclosed the suspect's name despite a lack of evidence.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:55.620
Consequently, the harassment against the suspect escalated.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:59.680
Eventually, it grew too much for her, and she stopped coming to school altogether.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.940
It was later discovered that the tip was fake all along,

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:08.030
and Oosawa was placed on probation for unjust investigation.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.640
President Mouri recently returned as the Public Safety Commissioner

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:13.700
and holds a concurrent post as Student Council President.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:18.010
Things calmed down a bit after President Mouri returned,

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:23.320
but the Public Safety Commission has never really cracked down on financial-aid student harassment.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.340
What you saw earlier is rare.

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.200
Oojima-senpai.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:34.380
Thank you so much for saving me earlier.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:37.100
Oh, no, I didn't do anything.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:40.500
That's not true. You came to help me, and that's more than enough.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.110
It was very encouraging.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.480
W-Was it?

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.200
Yes!

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:46.800
Glad I could help, then.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.340
You were really cool.

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.110
It's a shame that I didn't take any pictures.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.400
You flatter me...

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.780
Wasn't the financial aid system originally set up

00:14:54.780 --> 00:15:00.370
to assist students who excel academically but have financial troubles, like a relief fund?

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.380
Yes.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.500
The policy was adopted to increase the student population

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.920
without decreasing the school's academic achievement.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.020
The system deploys financial aid students to work at cooperating companies

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:12.890
and uses earnings from that to fund their tuition.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:16.540
And they're prohibited from working part-time so that they can focus on the work

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:17.960
assigned by the school.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.880
They can't join clubs, either.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:21.520
They're admirable, hardworking students.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.540
Financial aid students aren't doing anything to deserve harassment!

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:28.030
They should be proud of themselves!

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:35.500
Hey, Mii-chan. I want to add a policy to my manifesto.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:36.980
Will you consider it?

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:39.450
Sure. What is it?

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:45.380
I want to end the discrimination against financial aid students here at Takafuji High School!

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.160
Welcome back, ma'am.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:03.140
I feel like I'm an executive who was just discharged from prison or something.

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.060
Well, I guess that's exactly the case.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:06.760
Have you been well?

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:11.060
I have! But I had to stay at home while on probation, so I gained some.

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.140
Gained what?

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:14.700
Oh, don't you worry your little head over it.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.000
Okay...

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.820
Have <i>you</i> been well, Yakumo-senpai?

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:21.830
It must have been so much trouble having to manage two posts while I was away.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:25.620
Not at all. The Vice-President took care of most of the work.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:26.710
Oh.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:30.960
It was easier than dealing with me, since I'm with the Katahira faction.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:35.470
That's right. I've heard a bit about the election.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:40.470
Let me hear your take later.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:41.720
All right.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:47.840
I, Oosawa Yuina, have now returned as the Public Safety Commissioner.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.840
I'll do my best to live up to your expectations!

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.610
We're counting on your vote!

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:02.120
I almost mistook the Dog Pot Club for dog eaters.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.420
And isn't it weird that they're getting off with budget cuts

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:07.260
while the Food Club is getting shut down?

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.620
Hey, Yuuki...

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:09.480
What is it?

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:12.130
Is that what you really think?

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.820
Oh, I mean, every club has a reason to exist!

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.000
They shouldn't be forced to disband or cut their budgets!

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:18.890
Right?

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:23.810
Not that! I'm talking about adding the financial aid issue to your manifesto.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:25.520
Oh, that?

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:29.120
The reason we're in the election is to save the Food Club, right?

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.260
Yeah. What's your point?

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:32.400
Then why would you add a policy like that?

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:32.940
Huh?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:36.040
We need to win this election!

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:40.200
We need a manifesto that gets as many students to side with us as possible.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:43.900
Can't you see how badly the financial aid students are being harassed?

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:47.680
I can! And that's because the majority of the students look down on them!

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:52.050
That means your policy might make that majority turn their backs on you!

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.620
Financial aid students are the minority.

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.220
Policies benefiting minorities put you at a disadvantage!

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.200
But I can't neglect the issue, now can I?

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.800
Work on it <i>after</i> you get elected!

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:04.400
Right now, winning the election comes before anything else!

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:07.580
But there are people being harassed as we speak!

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:10.520
We need to bring attention to this issue as soon as we can!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.400
Stop it!

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:14.920
Are you so set on this because you want justice?

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:17.140
Or is it because Isara is a financial aid student?

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:17.820
What?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.700
Because you want to impress Hazuki?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.880
Because you want that ASP reporter to praise you?

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.450
Because you want to compete with the Finance Commissioner?

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:26.900
What's wrong, Chisato?

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.080
Don't leave me behind.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.640
Don't go anywhere.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:32.830
Chisato...

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:35.960
Why? Why are you leaving me behind?

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:37.960
I'm right here with you.

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:43.260
Then why do you feel so far away?

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:48.800
Why are we drifting apart,
when we were so close?

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.020
We're not drifting apart.

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:52.220
I tell you this all the time.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:54.420
I'll always be here for you.

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:55.530
I'm not going anywhere.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.280
I promise.

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:05.540
Oh, he's doing pretty well in the polls.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.420
He has the potential to win this election.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:13.040
So? Do you think he'll side with us?

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:16.380
Yes. His interests match ours.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:17.760
That's not what I mean.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:21.300
I'm wondering if he'll listen to me.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:23.400
He's amiable and enjoys interacting—

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.810
You're still not getting it.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:29.350
I'm asking whether he'll be a puppet president for the Public Safety Commission.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:32.220
Did I <i>have</i> to spell it out for you?

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:34.900
So, will he?

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:40.800
We are only cooperating with him so that he is elected.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.240
So he won't be our puppet!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:46.160
He's not on our side, then.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:52.220
He might institute policies that leave the Public Safety Commission at a disadvantage.

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:53.440
Oosawa-kun.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.840
You should know better than to team up with shady people, Senpai.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.740
They might slit your throat while you sleep.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:01.840
Or <i>I</i> might have to slit <i>his</i> throat.

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:04.820
Just kidding!

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.760
See you tomorrow.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.440
The new approval ratings are out!

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:19.220
According to the latest poll, although it's only by a narrow margin from Shinonome,

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:21.450
you have the highest rating among the candidates!

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:29.870
Let me see!

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:32.440
Is that data reliable?

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:48.010
What's up with that data? Why is his approval rating so high with the girls?

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.540
I'm sure they found Yuu-kun charming.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.160
It's Yuuki we're talking about!

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:55.020
There's a better chance of seeing pigs fly.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:56.680
That's harsh.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:04.150
That's the Recycling Club's car.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:05.980
The road hogs.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.830
Oojima.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:14.330
Aren't you gonna play that harmonica?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.040
I'm trying...

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:18.460
but it won't play.

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:21.380
Um, can I see it?

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:25.340
I wonder if it's broken.

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:28.960
Yuuki, what are you doing?!

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:29.540
Huh?

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:31.560
That's an indirect kiss.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:32.310
What?!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.020
Sorry, Morishita-san!

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.720
I didn't mean to!

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.340
It's okay...

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.360
if it's you.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.680
It's <i>not</i> okay!

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:43.540
And why are <i>you</i> blushing, Yuuki?!

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:46.570
No, it's not what you think! I didn't mean to...

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:48.140
What's "not what I think"?

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.240
It's like...

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:49.980
Like what?

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:51.660
Well, um, you know...

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:52.560
Run away!

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:53.760
Wait!

00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:09.340
No!

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:23.570
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:27.530
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:31.670
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:35.750
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:40.090
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:44.250
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:48.280
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:54.760
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:01.400
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:05.570
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:07.760
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:11.460
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.990
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:18.250
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:22.130
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:27.890
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:35.760
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:45.690
Yaoi Sticks taste good.

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:48.180
They come in quite a variety of flavors, don't they?

00:23:48.180 --> 00:23:50.860
The vast array of flavors amazes me.

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:55.700
By the way, what's the name of the character on this package?

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:57.080
Yaoemon.

00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:00.040
I must say, it's quite the original character.

00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:01.500
Normal.

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:05.480
Next time, Episode 10: "Complications!"

00:24:06.190 --> 00:24:07.320
Normal...

00:24:07.990 --> 00:24:09.180
but weird.
